„­bible_version£KJV¤book;§chapter¨sections•…¤book;§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢Likewise, ye wives, be in subjection to your own husbands; that, if any obey not the word, they also may without the word be won by the conversation of the wives;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ=while they behold your chaste conversation coupled with fear.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}Whose adorning let it not be that outward adorning of plaiting the hair, and of wearing of gold, or of putting on of apparel;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§but let it be the hidden man of the heart, in that which is not corruptible, even the ornament of a meek and quiet spirit, which is in the sight of God of great price.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor after this manner in the old time the holy women also, who trusted in God, adorned themselves, being in subjection unto their own husbands:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„even as Sara obeyed Abraham, calling him lord: whose daughters ye are, as long as ye do well, and are not afraid with any amazement.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book;§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙËLikewise, ye husbands, dwell with them according to knowledge, giving honour unto the wife, as unto the weaker vessel, and as being heirs together of the grace of life; that your prayers be not hindered.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book;§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmFinally, be ye all of one mind, having compassion one of another, love as brethren, be pitiful, be courteous:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜not rendering evil for evil, or railing for railing: but contrariwise blessing; knowing that ye are thereunto called, that ye should inherit a blessing.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
