„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!Let him eschew evil, and do good;¦layout ‚¤textÙ!Let him seek peace, and ensue it.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ0For the eyes of the Lord are over the righteous,¦layout ‚¤textÙ)And his ears are open unto their prayers:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ6But the face of the Lord is against them that do evil.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book;§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKAnd who is he that will harm you, if ye be followers of that which is good?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsBut and if ye suffer for righteousness' sake, happy are ye: and be not afraid of their terror, neither be troubled;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨but sanctify the Lord God in your hearts: and be ready always to give an answer to every man that asketh you a reason of the hope that is in you with meekness and fear:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšhaving a good conscience; that, whereas they speak evil of you, as of evildoers, they may be ashamed that falsely accuse your good conversation in Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_For it is better, if the will of God be so, that ye suffer for well doing, than for evil doing.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book;§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢For Christ also hath once suffered for sins, the just for the unjust, that he might bring us to God, being put to death in the flesh, but quickened by the Spirit:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ>by which also he went and preached unto the spirits in prison;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµwhich sometime were disobedient, when once the longsuffering of God waited in the days of Noah, while the ark was a preparing, wherein few, that is, eight souls were saved by water.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃThe like figure whereunto even baptism doth also now save us (not the putting away of the filth of the flesh, but the answer of a good conscience toward God,) by the resurrection of Jesus Christ:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxwho is gone into heaven, and is on the right hand of God; angels and authorities and powers being made subject unto him.¦layout ªlast_verse